      "@id": "https://kadi-dlr.hiu-batteries.de/records/9371#description",
      "@type": "Text",
      "encodingFormat": "text/markdown",
      "text": "# Scope\nThis record contains electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) measurements of the NMC cathode from an LG CHEM INR18650-MJ1 lithium-ion cell, structured for machine-readable applications. The dataset includes Parquet files with harmonized tabular impedance data, suitable for computational pipelines, and optionally linked data in JSON-LD format for semantic annotation. These measurements were recorded at 25°C and cover both charge and discharge sequences over the full SOC range.\n\n# Files\n## Data\n| Filename                                           | Description                                                             | Format               | Usage                                                             |\n|----------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 18650_LG_3500_MJ1_EIS_cathode_charge.parquet       | Structured impedance spectrum of NMC cathode at indicated SOC and 25°C. | application/parquet    | Use in data science pipelines or impedance modeling.             |\n| 18650_LG_3500_MJ1_EIS_cathode_discharge.parquet    | Structured impedance spectrum of NMC cathode at indicated SOC and 25°C. | application/parquet    | Use in data science pipelines or impedance modeling.             |\n\n## RDF Metadata\n| Filename                 | Description                                                          | Format             | Usage                                                                 |\n|--------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| metadata.jsonld|RDF metadata describing the data table schema, test, and battery | application/json+ld| Semantic Web integration|\n| metadata.html|RDF metadata describing the data table schema, test, and battery | application/json+ld| Semantic Web integration|\n\n# Licensing\nThis dataset is licensed under CC-BY 4.0, allowing for sharing and adaptation with proper attribution.\n\n# Contact Information\nFor questions or further assistance, please contact Dennis Kopljar at dennis.kopljar@dlr.de.\n\n# References\nThis dataset is linked to the following publication: [DOI/Link to publication]."
    },
